(rule/isolation_forest/lstm_ae/transformer/gnn columns above are BLENDED across all 3 devices -- only esp32-vib-001 has real IF/LSTM-AE/Transformer models, the other two devices mirror rule_score into those slots (see isolation_forest_scorer.py's docstring), so these columns measure 'what the live pipeline would actually see', not the sequence models' own standalone quality. See the FAIR COMPARISON block below for that.)

Fusion (0.698) < best individual signal, rule_score (0.921), on RAW aggregate accuracy. This is a deliberate, verified trade-off, not an undertrained model: the meta-learner is trained with class_weight='balanced' (train_fusion_meta_learner.py) specifically because an unweighted fit let the numerous easy normal/anomalous_shock/forged_signature examples dominate the decision boundary and effectively discard the GNN's signal on the rarer 'coordinated' attack type (verified: unweighted fused recall on 'coordinated' was 0.261, WORSE than gnn_score alone at 0.870 -- balancing recovers it, see the per-event-type table below and SESSION_LOG.md for the full before/after). Aggregate accuracy alone is the wrong single number to optimise for a security system where missing a rare coordinated attack is costlier than a few extra false positives on common, already-well-caught event types.

